  <revision rev="2" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>ac6912242e2510442b83fca5c689cae7</srcmd5>
    <version>0.4.14</version>
    <time>1787579029</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.4.14, and stop guessing a GPU vendor

Supersedes request 1373165, adding one patch on top of the same 0.4.14
update.

detect_vendor() looked for &quot;+cu&quot; or &quot;+rocm&quot; in the PyTorch version
string. Only upstream's own wheels carry that suffix, so a distribution
PyTorch never matched and init() then logged

  Could not autodetect AIMDO implementation, assuming Nvidia

on every ComfyUI start, for every user, whatever hardware they have. It
now reads the cuda and hip attributes that the same version module
already defines, and when PyTorch has neither it reports failure with an
informational message instead of naming a vendor it never selected. That
path is what happens here regardless, since the native allocator is not
built.

%check now exercises it. Local build green on both flavours, rpmlint clean.</comment>
    <requestid>1373273</requestid>
  </revision>
